From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:35:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 137/138] feat(refinery): wire acceptance-check into the patrol
 behind acceptance_check=off (gcp-s7j4.2)

acceptance-check.sh (gcp-s7j4.1) built a packet per bead and recorded a verdict,
but nothing called it. mol-refinery-patrol now has an acceptance-check step
between find-work and rebase (DESIGN section 2 on gcp-s7j4): a fence resolves the
pack's script the way merge-push does, fetches, and builds one packet per bead it
is about to merge (the head, and every member of a batch manifest). Each packet
is read against the rubric, DESIGN section 5 verbatim, and the verdict recorded.
A bead with nothing to read gets a SKIP record from the fence itself.

The var acceptance_check defaults to "off", which prints one line and does
nothing else. warn reads and records but never edits the manifest, rejects or
blocks a merge. reject runs as warn until gcp-s7j4.4. An unrendered placeholder,
empty or unknown value means off. rebase now needs acceptance-check, and
patrol-summary gains a bullet for the verdicts.

test_refinery_acceptance_wiring.sh proves the wiring by executing the extracted
fence under env -i in a real clone of a bare origin with a stub script, 13 cases,
and pins the fence, the prose and the rubric byte for byte so a changed word is a
failure. test_known_red_wiring.sh's want_steps gains the new step.

Validation: test_refinery_acceptance_wiring.sh, test_known_red_wiring.sh and
shellcheck pass. Mutating the fetch, the already-judged route, the off branch and
the stale-file cleanup each turns a case red.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
